  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1027 PM CST Sun Nov 22 2026\n\nGenerally quiet weather is expected from Wednesday through the rest \nof the week with drier northwest flow aloft returning in the wake of \nthe departing storm system. In contrast to earlier forecasts, model \nconsensus favors a repeating pattern of southwest surface flow each \nday Wednesday through Friday, which combined with modest midlevel \nheight rises will bring warmer temperatures for the days surrounding \nThanksgiving. The NBM bias correction scheme still has been slow to \ncatch onto this trend, but MOS guidance nevertheless shows some \npotential for highs to return to the 60s by the end of the week. At \nthis point, it looks like the upcoming weekend will also be dry and \nmild as the main storm track remains well to our north.",
